    title: "勒索軟體威脅升級：駭客集團開始實施家庭騷擾與實體暴力威脅",
    summary: "根據 Semperis 2026 年的報告數據，勒索軟體攻擊的威脅已從純數位層面擴展至實體安全。調查顯示，高達五分之一的受訪組織曾面臨威脅，且超過半數受訪者聲稱攻擊者已「實施了」其威脅。威脅內容包括騷擾、發送信件或包裹、威脅員工家人，甚至包括實體入侵、綁架和跟蹤。數據指出，威脅的實施情況在不同國家和產業垂直領域差異顯著，例如義大利的受害者報告了較高的綁架和身體傷害威脅。雖然 Semperis 報告基於自我回報，且缺乏獨立驗證的暴力攻擊案例，但文章指出駭客已透過「doxxing」（公開個人資料）和「swatting」（虛假警報）等方式將勒索行為個人化。此外，在加密貨幣竊盜領域，駭客也出現了「wrench attacks」（實體襲擊）等暴力行為。這顯示勒索威脅正在轉變為對受害者人身安全的真實風險，企業應提高警覺，並考慮制定包含實體安全防護的應變計畫。",
    tags: ["Ransomware", "實體威脅", "Semperis", "家庭騷擾", "Doxxing", "Cyber Extortion"],
    title_en: "Ransomware Threat Escalation: Hacker Groups Begin Implementing Harassment and Physical Violence Threats",
    summary_en: "According to Semperis's 2026 report data, the threat of ransomware attacks has expanded from purely digital dimensions to physical safety. The investigation found that up to one-fifth of surveyed organizations faced threats, and over half of respondents claimed that attackers had 'implemented' their threats. Threat content included harassment, sending mail or packages, threatening employee families, and even physical intrusion, kidnapping, and stalking. The data indicates significant variations in the implementation of threats across different countries and industry verticals; for example, victims in Italy reported higher threats of kidnapping and physical harm. Although the Semperis report is based on self-reported data and lacks independently verified cases of physical violence, the article points out that hackers are personalizing extortion through methods like 'doxxing' (publishing personal data) and 'swatting' (false alarms). Furthermore, in the cryptocurrency theft domain, hackers have also exhibited violent acts such as 'wrench attacks' (physical assaults). This demonstrates that ransomware threats are transforming into genuine risks to the physical safety of victims, urging enterprises to heighten their vigilance and consider developing incident response plans that include physical security defenses.",
    tags_en: ["Ransomware", "Physical Threats", "Semperis", "Family Harassment", "Doxxing", "Cyber Extortion"],
