    summary_en: "The large Dutch retail group Ahold Delhaize experienced a cybersecurity incident, affecting its main brands including Albert Heijn, Etos, and Gall & Gall. Following the incident, the company preemptively shut down certain systems on the afternoon of the 11th to protect its IT environment. This resulted in the disruption of online ordering, customer service, and some membership functions, leading to the cancellation of existing online orders. Beyond online services, physical stores were also impacted; Electronic Shelf Labels (ESL) were temporarily unable to update, potentially causing discrepancies between shelf prices and checkout prices. Furthermore, some logistics systems were temporarily shut down, affecting the supply of fresh produce. Ahold Delhaize issued a statement confirming the group's cybersecurity incident and stated that it has engaged external cybersecurity experts for an investigation. The company currently reports that there is no evidence of customer or employee data theft, but the extent of the impact varies, and the recovery of various systems is ongoing.",
