    title: "前 OpenAI 工程師涉嫌在辦公室安裝秘密錄音裝置，竊取公司機密資訊",
    summary: "美國司法部宣布，聯邦調查局（FBI）已逮捕一名涉嫌在OpenAI辦公室安裝秘密錄音裝置的工程師。該嫌犯為沙烏地阿拉伯籍男子Abdulrahman Alfozan，於10月9日被捕。根據調查，Alfozan自2025年7月擔任OpenAI工程師。OpenAI在9月30日例行安全檢查時，在高階主管會議室發現一個藏於電視機USB連接埠、並以衛生紙掩飾的秘密錄音裝置。該會議室討論的內容包含OpenAI尚未公開的技術進展、產品計畫、商業合作及政府往來等高度機密資訊。調查顯示，Alfozan曾多次在會議室附近徘徊，並利用生產力工具查詢辦公大樓、會議室位置及高階主管會議地點。此外，其相關帳號也曾多次詢問如何製作持續錄音裝置、改善監聽設備及加密SD記憶卡。OpenAI表示，已將案件移交FBI，並利用自家AI模型分析了錄音裝置及其來源。目前公司確認模型權重、原始碼或客戶資料並未遭未經授權存取或外洩，涉案員工已遭解雇。",
    tags: ["OpenAI", "FBI", "秘密錄音裝置", "內部威脅", "機密資訊竊取", "Abdulrahman Alfozan"],
    title_en: "Former OpenAI Engineer Suspected of Installing Secret Recording Devices in Office to Steal Company Secrets",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Department of Justice announced that the FBI has arrested an engineer suspected of installing secret recording devices in an OpenAI office. The suspect is Saudi national Abdulrahman Alfozan, who was apprehended on October 9. According to the investigation, Alfozan was employed as an OpenAI engineer starting in July 2025. During a routine security check on September 30, OpenAI discovered a secret recording device hidden in a TV's USB port and disguised with toilet paper in a senior executive conference room. The discussions held in that room included highly confidential information, such as OpenAI's unreleased technological advancements, product plans, business collaborations, and government dealings. The investigation revealed that Alfozan had repeatedly loitered near the conference room and used productivity tools to query the office building, conference room locations, and senior executive meeting spots. Furthermore, his related accounts repeatedly inquired about how to build continuous recording devices, improve listening equipment, and encrypt SD memory cards. OpenAI stated that it has handed the case over to the FBI and utilized its own AI models to analyze the recording device and its source. The company confirmed that its model weights, source code, or customer data were not accessed or leaked without authorization. The employee involved has been terminated.",
