    category: "Windows",
    title: "微軟發布 Windows 11 更新 KB5127648，修復遊戲中導致滑鼠輸入卡頓的系統 Bug",
    summary: "微軟透過 2026 年 10 月的 Patch Tuesday 更新 KB5127648，確認並修復了 Windows 11 系統中可能導致部分遊戲場景出現滑鼠輸入卡頓（stutter）的 Bug。此修復已包含在 KB5127648 的發行說明中，屬於系統層面的問題，而非使用者設備或驅動程式的責任。文章指出，此問題已引起遊戲玩家的關注，曾有用戶報告在《Star Wars: The Old Republic》和《Final Fantasy XIV》等遊戲中遇到滑鼠異常，甚至懷疑是系統更新導致。雖然微軟並未公開說明卡頓的確切原因或受影響的遊戲範圍，但修補程式的發布證實了問題出在 Windows 系統本身。建議受影響的用戶應立即安裝 KB5127648 安全更新，並重新啟動電腦。若更新後仍有卡頓，則可能需檢查周邊設備（如滑鼠、USB、GPU 驅動）或使用擴充基座（dock）是否為潛在的干擾源。",
    tags: ["Windows 11", "KB5127648", "Patch Tuesday", "Windows Update", "系統 Bug", "遊戲效能"],
    title_en: "Microsoft Releases Windows 11 Update KB5127648 to Fix System Bug Causing Mouse Input Stutter During Gaming",
    summary_en: "Microsoft released the KB5127648 update during the October 2026 Patch Tuesday, confirming and fixing a bug in Windows 11 that could cause mouse input stuttering in certain game scenarios. This fix, detailed in the KB5127648 release notes, addresses a system-level issue, rather than being attributable to user hardware or drivers. The article notes that this issue has drawn attention from gamers, with users reporting abnormal mouse behavior in games such as *Star Wars: The Old Republic* and *Final Fantasy XIV*, even suspecting system updates as the cause. Although Microsoft has not publicly disclosed the exact cause of the stuttering or the full scope of affected games, the patch's release confirms the problem resides within the Windows system itself. Affected users are advised to immediately install the KB5127648 security update and restart their computers. If stuttering persists after the update, users may need to check peripheral devices (such as mice, USB ports, or GPU drivers) or determine if a docking station is a potential source of interference.",
    tags_en: ["Windows 11", "KB5127648", "Patch Tuesday", "Windows Update", "System Bug", "Gaming Performance"],
