    title: "CISA警告兩高風險漏洞遭積極利用，要求聯邦機構於三日內修補",
    summary: "美國網路安全與基礎設施安全局（CISA）於10月13日發布警告，指出已掌握兩項資安漏洞遭到積極利用的證據，並將其列入已遭利用的漏洞名單（KEV）。受影響的漏洞包括 Windows 命令注入漏洞 CVE-2026-96951，以及 Ivanti Connect Secure (ICS) 的身分驗證繞過漏洞 CVE-2026-104935。CISA已要求所有聯邦機構必須在極短的期限內，即10月16日之前，緊急進行修補作業。這兩項漏洞的發現，強調了攻擊者對關鍵基礎設施的持續威脅，要求機構必須立即採取行動，修補這些已知的、且正在被積極利用的漏洞，以降低被駭的風險。",
    tags: ["CISA", "CVE-2026-96951", "CVE-2026-104935", "Ivanti Connect Secure", "Windows", "KEV"],
    title_en: "CISA Warns of Two High-Risk Vulnerabilities Being Actively Exploited, Mandating Federal Agency Patching Within Three Days",
    summary_en: "The Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) issued a warning on October 13th, stating that it has evidence of two vulnerabilities being actively exploited and listing them on its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog. The affected vulnerabilities include the Windows command injection vulnerability CVE-2026-96951, and the Ivanti Connect Secure (ICS) authentication bypass vulnerability CVE-2026-104935. CISA has mandated that all federal agencies must urgently patch these vulnerabilities by October 16th. The discovery of these two flaws emphasizes the ongoing threat to critical infrastructure from attackers, requiring agencies to take immediate action to patch these known, actively exploited vulnerabilities to mitigate the risk of compromise.",
